#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054384 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054654 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b170bf27-76bc-5558-9133-e81a4760072f" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Linear Equations that Involve Multiplication"}] :question/id #uuid "8955a3ce-a161-5dc5-8ec0-c357a0403b46" :question/math-academy-id "e-12862" :question/problem "Solve the equation $3p-7 =20.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we apply the addition principle, adding $7$ to both sides:\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n    \t\t3p-7 &=20\\\n\t\t3p-7+7 &=20+7 \\\n                3p + 0 &= 27 \\\n\t\t3p &=27\n\t}\n$$\n\nSecond, we apply the multiplication principle, dividing both sides by $3\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t3p &=27 \\[5pt]\n\t\t\\dfrac{3p}{3} &=\\dfrac{27}{3} \\[5pt]  \n\t\t\\dfrac{\\cancel{3}p}{\\cancel{3}} &= 9 \\[5pt]  \n\t\tp &=9\n\t}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054385 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054655 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "52c2b31a-9b7a-52cb-9fa7-111de8bc53ea" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Linear Equations while Keeping the Variable on the Right-Hand Side"}] :question/id #uuid "074b5213-4f4e-5d1b-a5c4-8b5403901b4d" :question/math-academy-id "e-12863" :question/problem "Solve for $x$ where $2=5x-8.$" :question/worked-solution "To save time, we will keep the variable on the right-hand side as we solve. First, we apply the addition principle, adding $8$ to both sides:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2 & =5x-8 \\\\ 2+8 & =5x-8+8 \\\\ 10 & =5x+0 \\\\ 10 & =5x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSecond, we apply the multiplication principle, dividing both sides by $5\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}10 & =5x \\\\ \\frac{10}{5} & =\\frac{5x}{5} \\\\ 2 & =\\frac{\\cancel{5}x}{\\cancel{5}} \\\\ 2 & =x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $2=x,$ we conclude that the solution is $x=2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054386 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054656 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ac53e171-0a02-5b74-8a3a-465dbecda9d7" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Linear Equations that Involve Division"}] :question/id #uuid "1f5b9030-a5de-5ac2-95c4-2fbaf638cdab" :question/math-academy-id "e-12864" :question/problem "Solve the equation $7-\\dfrac{p}{3} =9.$" :question/worked-solution "After converting the equation to a more familiar form, we apply the addition principle, subtracting $7$ from both sides:\n\n$$\n\\require{cancel}\n\t\\eqalign{\n               7-\\dfrac{p}{3} &=9 \\\n    \t\t-\\dfrac{p}{3}+7 &=9\\\n\t\t-\\dfrac{p}{3}+7-7 &= 9-7 \\\n\t\t-\\dfrac{p}{3}+0 &= 2 \\\n\t\t-\\dfrac{p}{3} &=2\n\t}\n$$\n\nThen, we apply the multiplication principle. We multiply by $-1$ to get rid of the negative sign, and again by $3$ to get rid of the fraction:\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n               -\\dfrac{p}{3} &=2 \\\n              (-1) \\cdot \\left( -\\dfrac{p}{3} \\right) &=(-1) \\cdot 2 \\\n\t\t\\dfrac{p}{3} &=-2 \\\n\t\t\\cancel{3} \\cdot \\dfrac{p}{\\cancel{3}} &=3 \\cdot (-2) \\   \n\t\tp &=-6\n\t}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054387 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054657 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "82077653-3463-5132-b0a9-8376fdb47319" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Linear Equations that Involve Fractions"}] :question/id #uuid "6ed7ae7f-2591-5747-9fa0-933260aaaebf" :question/math-academy-id "e-12866" :question/problem "Solve the equation $-\\dfrac{z}{3}-\\dfrac 1 2 =\\dfrac 7 2.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we apply the addition principle, adding $\\dfrac{1}{2}$ to both sides:\n\n$$\n\\require{cancel}\n\t\\eqalign{\n    \t\t-\\dfrac{z}{3}-\\dfrac 1 2 &=\\dfrac 7 2\\[5pt]\n\t\t-\\dfrac{z}{3} - \\dfrac 1 2+\\dfrac 1 2 &= \\dfrac 7 2+\\dfrac 1 2 \\[5pt]\n-\\dfrac{z}{3} + 0 &= \\dfrac 7 2+\\dfrac 1 2 \\[5pt]\n\t\t-\\dfrac{z}{3} &=\\dfrac 8 2 \\[5pt]\n\t\t-\\dfrac{z}{3} &=4\n\t}\n$$\n\nThen, we apply the multiplication principle. We multiply by $-1$ to get rid of the negative sign, and again by $3$ to get rid of the fraction.\n\n$$\n\\require{cancel}\n\t\\eqalign{\n-\\dfrac{z}{3} &=4 \\\n(-1) \\cdot \\left( -\\dfrac{z}{3} \\right) &= (-1) \\cdot 4 \\[5pt]\n\t\t\\dfrac{z}{3} &=-4 \\[5pt]\n\t\t\\cancel{3} \\cdot \\dfrac{z}{\\cancel{3}} &= 3 \\cdot (-4) \\[5pt]   \n\t\tz &=-12\n\t}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186486411 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054654 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b170bf27-76bc-5558-9133-e81a4760072f" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Linear Equations that Involve Multiplication"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "95b1c53a-0aab-5610-b822-d25de288ff5c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486035}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "95b1c53a-0aab-5610-b822-d25de288ff5c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486035} :answer-field/id #uuid "174910db-42d0-5880-b404-dbc2110a0bba" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486246}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "8eb9e3bf-e422-579f-aaa8-f647ba12c4ce" :question/math-academy-id "q-175701" :question/problem "If $-2y-6=10$, then $y=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "First, we apply the addition principle, adding $6$ to both sides:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2y-6 & =10 \\\\ -2y-6+6 & =10+6 \\\\ -2y+0 & =16 \\\\ -2y & =16\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSecond, we apply the multiplication principle, dividing both sides by $-2:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2y & =16 \\\\ \\frac{-2y}{-2} & =\\frac{16}{-2} \\\\ \\frac{\\cancel{-2}y}{\\cancel{-2}} & =-8 \\\\ y & =-8\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186486386 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054655 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "52c2b31a-9b7a-52cb-9fa7-111de8bc53ea" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Linear Equations while Keeping the Variable on the Right-Hand Side"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c1317bf7-636a-5d47-b987-01bc1bc04414" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486111}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c1317bf7-636a-5d47-b987-01bc1bc04414" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486111} :answer-field/id #uuid "289c2c69-8b42-5177-bf1b-2bc87e91269d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486250}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5a23d8ac-15ec-5a10-9024-19b8ee7d9529" :question/math-academy-id "q-175704" :question/problem "If $23=3+5x,$ then $x=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "To save time, we will keep the variable on the right-hand side as we solve. First, we rewrite the right-hand side by placing the term containing the variable first:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}23 & =3+5x \\\\ 23 & =5x+3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we apply the addition principle, subtracting $3$ from both sides:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}23 & =5x+3 \\\\ 23-3 & =5x+3-3 \\\\ 20 & =5x+0 \\\\ 20 & =5x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we apply the multiplication principle, dividing both sides by $5:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}20 & =5x \\\\ \\frac{20}{5} & =\\frac{5x}{5} \\\\ 4 & =\\frac{\\cancel{5}x}{\\cancel{5}} \\\\ 4 & =x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $4=x,$ we conclude that the solution is $x=4.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186486398 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054656 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ac53e171-0a02-5b74-8a3a-465dbecda9d7" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Linear Equations that Involve Division"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b6e4eb07-e8cb-58d0-804f-3e01891dec9c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486095}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b6e4eb07-e8cb-58d0-804f-3e01891dec9c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486095} :answer-field/id #uuid "990fc942-5942-5a32-a9d4-3cfed01570f8" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486302}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "72bfe419-b757-596f-a22c-c1bac378d986" :question/math-academy-id "q-175711" :question/problem "If $\\frac{1}{2}x-3=7,$ then $x=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "First, we apply the addition principle, adding $3$ to both sides:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}x-3 & =7 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}x-3+3 & =7+3 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}x+0 & =10 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}x & =10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSecond, we apply the multiplication principle, multiplying both sides by $2:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}x & =10 \\\\ \\cancel{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\cancel{2}}x & =2\\cdot 10 \\\\ x & =20\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186486396 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054657 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "82077653-3463-5132-b0a9-8376fdb47319" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Linear Equations that Involve Fractions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a5150305-f633-5c03-a1ea-cf47770c77f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{16}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486061}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a5150305-f633-5c03-a1ea-cf47770c77f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{16}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486061} :answer-field/id #uuid "d71f5583-5918-5550-9ce3-fae2e571455e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486326}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "70ef95c9-ed21-5658-8a26-f0325d14f5de" :question/math-academy-id "q-175715" :question/problem "If $\\frac{x}{2}-3=-\\frac{1}{3},$ then $x=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "First, we apply the addition principle, adding $3$ to both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x}{2}-3 & =-\\frac{1}{3} \\\\ \\frac{x}{2}-3+3 & =-\\frac{1}{3}+3 \\\\ \\frac{x}{2}+0 & =-\\frac{1}{3}+\\frac{9}{3} \\\\ \\frac{x}{2} & =\\frac{8}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we apply the multiplication principle, multiplying both sides of the equation by $2:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x}{2} & =\\frac{8}{3} \\\\ \\cancel{2}\\cdot \\frac{x}{\\cancel{2}} & =2\\cdot \\frac{8}{3} \\\\ x & =\\frac{16}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186486391 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054654 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b170bf27-76bc-5558-9133-e81a4760072f" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Linear Equations that Involve Multiplication"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "06277756-fc24-5507-b919-b617ef820898" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485777}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "06277756-fc24-5507-b919-b617ef820898" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485777} :answer-field/id #uuid "1bc8c069-3b50-5073-99bf-4aedd4be9224" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486247}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "601f830e-c315-59b5-a69c-03f1a29eaaa7" :question/math-academy-id "q-177723" :question/problem "If $-x+9=7$, then $x=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "First, we apply the addition principle, subtracting $9$ from both sides:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-x+9 & =7 \\\\ -x+9-9 & =7-9 \\\\ -x+0 & =-2 \\\\ -x & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSecond, we apply the multiplication principle. We multiply by $-1$ to get rid of the negative sign.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-x & =-2 \\\\ (-1)\\cdot (-x) & =(-1)\\cdot (-2) \\\\ x & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186486394 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054656 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ac53e171-0a02-5b74-8a3a-465dbecda9d7" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Linear Equations that Involve Division"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bedf5288-f50d-5cd7-955a-3a7710b18df4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486106}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bedf5288-f50d-5cd7-955a-3a7710b18df4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486106} :answer-field/id #uuid "ada292af-bf5d-5b1f-b7aa-b319a67479c5" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486310}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6c613ffa-a60b-5471-88b3-f5e630584f18" :question/math-academy-id "q-177743" :question/problem "If $\\frac{1}{7}x-5=-4,$ then $x=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "First, we apply the addition principle, adding $5$ to both sides:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{7}x-5 & =-4 \\\\ \\frac{1}{7}x-5+5 & =-4+5 \\\\ \\frac{1}{7}x+0 & =1 \\\\ \\frac{1}{7}x & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSecond, we apply the multiplication principle, multiplying both sides by $7:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{7}x & =1 \\\\ \\cancel{7}\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\cancel{7}}x & =7\\cdot 1 \\\\ x & =7\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186055179 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054657 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "82077653-3463-5132-b0a9-8376fdb47319" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Linear Equations that Involve Fractions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a6831d18-43ec-5dd7-b0d7-b96de99de3d4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{10}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186052371} {:answer/id #uuid "e8799bb3-58d5-50d8-99ec-06232fb5986f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{10}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186052372} {:answer/id #uuid "ff6b8afa-5a1c-569d-bf7b-19d0f2a18923" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{20}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186052373} {:answer/id #uuid "3d27a309-0bbf-5fcd-9a6b-c774eac2658f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186052374} {:answer/id #uuid "65763377-79b8-5e41-b68f-947b8ca32f35" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{20}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186052375}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "65763377-79b8-5e41-b68f-947b8ca32f35" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{20}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186052375} :answer-field/id #uuid "8ad4a929-789a-52ff-93db-ed9f973cda83" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186052370}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b53aeb0c-2291-515b-8b32-fdcd601499c7" :question/math-academy-id "q-2540" :question/problem "If $\\frac{x}{5}+2=\\frac{2}{3}$, then $x=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we apply the addition principle, subtracting $2$ from both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x}{5}+2 & =\\frac{2}{3} \\\\ \\frac{x}{5}+2-2 & =\\frac{2}{3}-2 \\\\ \\frac{x}{5}+0 & =\\frac{2}{3}-\\frac{6}{3} \\\\ \\frac{x}{5} & =-\\frac{4}{3}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we apply the multiplication principle, multiplying both sides of the equation by $5:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x}{5} & =-\\frac{4}{3} \\\\ \\cancel{5}\\cdot \\frac{x}{\\cancel{5}} & =5\\cdot (-\\frac{4}{3}) \\\\ x & =-\\frac{20}{3}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186486417 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054655 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "52c2b31a-9b7a-52cb-9fa7-111de8bc53ea" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Linear Equations while Keeping the Variable on the Right-Hand Side"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "28a7a6f3-5966-516c-8785-4c6839f475c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485834} {:answer/id #uuid "87e6b7af-ba77-5346-b1ea-81d516760b33" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{11}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486002} {:answer/id #uuid "8a0063b3-6d51-5d4b-8a74-31e077922d3c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486010} {:answer/id #uuid "b0df784a-68b5-5fbc-b71a-54de7c737809" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486082} {:answer/id #uuid "f3a1a01b-6be2-5722-acec-37ba4536d61d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{9}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486207}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "28a7a6f3-5966-516c-8785-4c6839f475c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485834} :answer-field/id #uuid "955d647b-ec6b-5f54-8cf0-43b3e20b6401" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486300}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "981f6277-663e-5d5c-beb0-98c4f0b0b4d5" :question/math-academy-id "q-58208" :question/problem "Solve for $y$ where $16=3y+1.$" :question/worked-solution "To save time, we will keep the variable on the right-hand side as we solve. First, we apply the addition principle, subtracting $1$ from both sides:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}16 & =3y+1 \\\\ 16-1 & =3y+1-1 \\\\ 15 & =3y+0 \\\\ 15 & =3y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSecond, we apply the multiplication principle, dividing both sides by $3:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}15 & =3y \\\\ \\frac{15}{3} & =\\frac{3y}{3} \\\\ 5 & =\\frac{\\cancel{3}y}{\\cancel{3}} \\\\ 5 & =y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $5=y,$ we conclude that the solution is $y=5.$"}]}
